\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Two examples of Minari usage. \textbf  {Top:} Creating a Minari dataset using the Gymnasium wrapper. Non-Gymnasium environments are also supported and can be created manually via \lstinline |minari.create_dataset_from_buffers()|. \textbf  {Bottom:} Loading an existing dataset (local or remote). In many cases one can instead directly use one of the integrations with existing Offline RL libraries described in Sec.~\ref {sec:integrations}.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
